From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@compiler>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8996: add the APSS watchdog

msm8996.dtsi has no node for the APSS watchdog at 0x09830000, so
qcom-wdt never binds. On the ZTE Axon 7 the multi-boot shim arms this
watchdog (bark = bite = 30 s) before it starts LineageOS, as the
downstream kernel's msm_watchdog takes it over; a mainline kernel without
the node was reset ~30 s after boot without any log (M0a' test,
2026-11-10). With the node, qcom-wdt finds the watchdog running and the
watchdog core keeps it fed (WATCHDOG_HANDLE_BOOT_ENABLED) until userspace
opens /dev/watchdog.

Bark interrupt SPI 28 as in the downstream device tree (qcom,wdt@9830000:
interrupts <0 28 0>, <0 29 0>); clocked from the 32 kHz sleep clock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i64chehV1XxwjxyaGp
---
diff --color -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
@@ -3736,6 +3736,13 @@
 			#clock-cells = <0>;
 		};
 
+		watchdog@9830000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,apss-wdt-msm8996", "qcom,kpss-wdt";
+			reg = <0x09830000 0x1000>;
+			clocks = <&sleep_clk>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 28 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		};
+
 		timer@9840000 {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <1>;
diff --color -ruN a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/qcom-wdt.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/qcom-wdt.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/qcom-wdt.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/qcom-wdt.yaml
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
               - qcom,apss-wdt-msm8226
               - qcom,apss-wdt-msm8974
               - qcom,apss-wdt-msm8994
+              - qcom,apss-wdt-msm8996
               - qcom,apss-wdt-nord
               - qcom,apss-wdt-qcm2290
               - qcom,apss-wdt-qcs404
